WEBVTT

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:09.869
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Friday the eighteenth of September. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:19.460
<v Olumide Adeyemi>We can hear you. I'm less functional than the audio, mind. The broken coffee machine in the canteen has finished me off.</v>

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:24.859
<v Jamie Brennan>That coffee was mostly a threat anyway. You're probably better off.</v>

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:32.770
<v Tomasz Nowak>Between that and the football last night, not a brilliant start. How do you miss from there?</v>

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.700
<v David Whitfield>Years of practice, presumably.</v>

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:42.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get the full match analysis, let's separate the finished stuff from what actually needs doing.</v>

00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:49.880
<v Sarah Okafor>We tested the Gas Turbine 1 yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done.</v>

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:55.170
<v David Whitfield>Good. So that one's a closed item, not another job coming round.</v>

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.649
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I finished the repair on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel last night. That's complete as well.</v>

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:07.450
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. We also finished the repair on the Stretch Wrapper last night.</v>

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:13.849
<v Fiona Doyle>That repair's finished, then? Just keeping the completed entries separate from today's list.</v>

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Completed repair, not something we're assigning again.</v>

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:26.620
<v David Whitfield>One observation from me: heard a slight rattle from the Line 3 Chiller, nothing to action yet. Just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:30.010
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Observation only, no new job off that.</v>

00:01:31.859 --> 00:01:38.159
<v Jamie Brennan>And I'm still waiting on parts for the Site Water System, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.739
<v Fiona Doyle>So still blocked. Nothing executable there today.</v>

00:01:43.219 --> 00:01:46.019
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, exactly. Same position, not a fresh request.</v>

00:01:46.379 --> 00:01:52.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace Liu, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the wrapper this afternoon? It's urgent.</v>

00:01:53.939 --> 00:02:00.239
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the wrapper this afternoon. Understood on the urgency.</v>

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.510
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, talking over you—both bits, yeah? Not just getting the jam out?</v>

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:13.330
<v Grace Liu>Both bits. Clear the jam, then check the sensors. That's what I'm taking on.</v>

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:17.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace Liu. That's the urgent one for this afternoon.</v>

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:24.500
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, separate from the repair we've just closed. I was about to muddle those entries.</v>

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:28.360
<v Grace Liu>Yep, today's commitment is the jam and the sensor checks.</v>

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:34.050
<v Sarah Okafor>We've also got the monthly fire alarm test still needing an owner.</v>

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:43.439
<v Jamie Brennan>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test by the 28th. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Jamie Brennan. By the 28th, agreed.</v>

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.310
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, that's mine.</v>

00:02:51.539 --> 00:02:56.789
<v Grace Liu>That priority makes sense. Not an emergency doesn't mean it can disappear off the list.</v>

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:04.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, can you do a site visit at the warehouse with the contractor? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:13.830
<v Tomasz Nowak>The visit with the contractor, yeah? Not taking on any repair work off the back of that in this meeting?</v>

00:03:15.729 --> 00:03:20.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Just the site visit at the warehouse with the contractor. That's the scope.</v>

00:03:21.199 --> 00:03:25.050
<v Tomasz Nowak>Okay, I'll do that. It matters but it's not urgent, understood.</v>

00:03:26.699 --> 00:03:30.900
<v Fiona Doyle>And there's no time or date being agreed for that here, correct?</v>

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:35.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Don't put a deadline in that we haven't agreed.</v>

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:42.939
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I'll grease and check the bearings on the air compressor tomorrow at 9:30. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:44.919 --> 00:03:48.419
<v Tomasz Nowak>Tomorrow as in Saturday? Sorry, my brain's still on Thursday.</v>

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:53.780
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Saturday, yeah. Tomorrow at 9:30, grease and check the bearings on the air compressor.</v>

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Olumide. Normal priority for that.</v>

00:03:58.389 --> 00:04:01.189
<v David Whitfield>Right, not being presented as a breakdown, then.</v>

00:04:02.539 --> 00:04:04.990
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, normal priority. That's all I'm saying.</v>

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:12.030
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll schedule downtime for the water booster with production at half two. Low priority.</v>

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:22.230
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona, just so we don't cross wires: at half two you're doing the scheduling with production, not saying the downtime itself starts then?</v>

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:28.829
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. At half two I'll schedule it with production. We haven't agreed a downtime window here.</v>

00:04:30.899 --> 00:04:35.449
<v Jamie Brennan>Got you. I heard half two and thought it was going off then.</v>

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.509
<v Fiona Doyle>No, just the scheduling. Low priority, as I said.</v>

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:49.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Next one: the sensors on the air dryer need recalibrating today at 2pm. The priority cue is no rush. Anyone able to own that?</v>

00:04:50.939 --> 00:04:56.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I can't take that one on. Don't put me against it just because it's sensors.</v>

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.300
<v Grace Liu>No, I can't commit to that either.</v>

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:05.850
<v Fiona Doyle>So the air dryer recalibration still says today at 2pm, no rush, but there's no owner?</v>

00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:11.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. That's the requirement as raised, but nobody's accepted it. It stays unowned.</v>

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:24.360
<v David Whitfield>There's also the need to book a contractor to look at the Injection Moulding Line 3 tomorrow morning. Normal priority. That's the booking due tomorrow morning, not a confirmed visit. Anyone taking it?</v>

00:05:26.019 --> 00:05:29.519
<v Jamie Brennan>Not me, I'm afraid. I can't commit to that booking.</v>

00:05:31.209 --> 00:05:37.160
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't take that either. My contractor visit at the warehouse is separate; it doesn't cover this.</v>

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:45.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Booking a contractor to look at the Injection Moulding Line 3, tomorrow morning, normal priority—still nobody taking ownership.</v>

00:05:47.209 --> 00:05:52.810
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, those last two are unowned requirements. Not agreed commitments from anyone, and definitely not completed.</v>

00:05:54.759 --> 00:05:58.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Anything else that's just a status update rather than another job?</v>

00:06:01.209 --> 00:06:04.709
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, that's my lot. And no more football analysis, apparently.</v>

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.579
<v David Whitfield>Nothing else. The rattle I mentioned is only an observation, just to be clear.</v>

00:06:12.339 --> 00:06:17.240
<v Jamie Brennan>Same here. Parts are still the blocker on the item I mentioned; no change.</v>

00:06:19.459 --> 00:06:26.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we've got the accepted work and the two unowned items clearly separated. Everyone happy that's what we've actually agreed?</v>

00:06:27.269 --> 00:06:33.220
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, all clear. Apart from the coffee situation, but that's a personal tragedy, not a job request.</v>

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:37.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Duly sympathised with. Thanks, everyone. We'll leave it there.</v>
